# RAW sources only. 738 MB of fetched upstream data: ŠÚ SR cubes, Eurostat bulk
# TSVs, OECD extracts, UN DESA tables, census files, PDFs. Not redistributed, and
# each publisher's own terms apply. Re-fetch with pipeline.run_stage1.
/data/raw/
/data/interim/

# data/processed/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is 656 KB of derived output and
# committing it is what makes the analysis layer runnable from a bare clone:
# without it, chart_data.py, headline_figures.py and validate/invariants.py have
# no input, because their input is generated from the 738 MB above. Verified: with
# data/processed/ present and data/raw/ absent, all three run.
#
# The only step that still needs raw is analysis/mirror_comparison.py, which reads
# the Eurostat TSVs directly; its output (mirror_comparison.json) is committed, so
# the figures survive even where the script cannot re-run.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
.astro/
.env
.env.local
pipeline/logs/
*.log
.DS_Store
